42.jpg (1.97 MB)" loading=lazy> </a></div></div></div></div><div id=chatlog__message-container-1468903473922707600 class=chatlog__message-container data-message-id=1468903473922707600><div class=chatlog__message><div class=chatlog__message-aside><div class=chatlog__short-timestamp title="Thursday, February 5, 2026 1:37 PM">1:37 PM</div></div><div class=chatlog__message-primary><div class="chatlog__content chatlog__markdown"><span class=chatlog__markdown-preserve><strong>Blinds Replacement Request and Landlord Approval Process — 12/09/2024</strong>

Stephen Cooke contacted the managing agent of 7A Bakeri Circuit, Warabrook, seeking guidance on replacing multiple sets of blinds throughout the rental property. He provided detailed measurements for each room, proposed adjusted dimensions to ensure proper fit, and included supporting photos and files for reference. He noted the existing blinds were partly aged with visible staining resembling mold, raising concerns due to his children’s health. While willing to cover the upfront cost, Stephen proposed that the landlord consider reimbursement at the end of the lease, as the improvements would enhance the property. The agent responded that a supplier should confirm measurements and requested a formal quote for landlord approval, while cautioning about potential costs. Alternative suppliers were suggested, and Stephen agreed to investigate options and proceed accordingly.</span> <span class=chatlog__edited-timestamp title="Thursday, May 14, 2026 11:39 AM">(edited)</span></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1468903473943674963/Window_Blinds_Replacement_for_Improved_Property_Condition_and_Hygiene.pdf?ex=6a2dcdb7&amp;is=6a2c7c37&amp;hm=fd18527732db5979760d1e18eb6830e2817859b57a33efcfdaf8518672d93b67&amp;"> Window_Blinds_Replacement_for_Improved_Property_Condition_and_Hygiene.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>407.73 KB</div></div></div></div></div></div></div>
<div class=chatlog__message-group><div id=chatlog__message-container-1468905307705970820 class=chatlog__message-container data-message-id=1468905307705970820><div class=chatlog__message><div class=chatlog__message-aside><img class=chatlog__avatar src=https://cdn.discordapp.com/embed/avatars/4.png alt=Avatar loading=lazy></div><div class=chatlog__message-primary><div class=chatlog__header><span class=chatlog__author title=dadventuressteve data-user-id=1264035953933156432>Veilocity</span> <span class=chatlog__timestamp title="Thursday, February 5, 2026 1:45 PM"><a href=#chatlog__message-container-1468905307705970820>2/5/2026 1:45 PM</a></span></div><div class="chatlog__content chatlog__markdown"><span class=chatlog__markdown-preserve><strong>Mediation Preparation Correspondence – Discussion Paper, Financial Proposals and Participation Requirements — Cooke &amp; Cooke (NCC3896/2023) — 27/06/2024</strong>

Mediation is confirmed for 27 June 2024 in Adamstown (Delaney Roberts offices). Matthew Shepherd prepared a Mediation Discussion Paper including the draft balance sheet, property orders (initial $200,000 payment, Merewether sale split, possible Southport sale fallback) and a spousal maintenance proposal of $1,200/week for 2 years. Before sending to the mediator and other side, he needs Stephen to sign the mediation participation agreement and confirm funds held in trust, including $3,850 (half mediator fee) plus $5,500 legal fees.</span> <span class=chatlog__edited-timestamp title="Thursday, May 14, 2026 8:21 PM">(edited)</span></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1468905307731132581/Private_Mediation_Preparation_Discussion_Paper_and_Trust_Funds_27_June_2024.pdf?ex=6a2dcf6c&amp;is=6a2c7dec&amp;hm=d5b108fa6bb700a00b0f48b6e4c140fbf71b06fc643e17cc0ed4c9bbbac1214e&amp;"> Private_Mediation_Preparation_Discussion_Paper_and_Trust_Funds_27_June_2024.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>968.77 KB</div></div></div></div></div></div></div>
<div class=chatlog__message-group><div id=chatlog__message-container-1468909555508445194 class=chatlog__message-container data-message-id=1468909555508445194><div class=chatlog__message><div class=chatlog__message-aside><img class=chatlog__avatar src=https://cdn.discordapp.com/embed/avatars/4.png alt=Avatar loading=lazy></div><div class=chatlog__message-primary><div class=chatlog__header><span class=chatlog__author title=dadventuressteve data-user-id=1264035953933156432>Veilocity</span> <span class=chatlog__timestamp title="Thursday, February 5, 2026 2:02 PM"><a href=#chatlog__message-container-1468909555508445194>2/5/2026 2:02 PM</a></span></div><div class="chatlog__content chatlog__markdown"><span class=chatlog__markdown-preserve><strong>Address Discrepancy Correspondence – Tenancy and Utility Records Misalignment — Warabrook NSW — 04/12/2025</strong>

AGL’s final electricity bill lists the supply address as U1/7 Bakeri Circuit, Warabrook NSW 2304, while the Residential Tenancy Agreement and Condition Report identify the premises as 7A Bakeri Cct, Warabrook NSW 2304. This inconsistency in the legal/property description is concerning and raises questions as to whether the tenancy and utility accounts were correctly aligned to the same dwelling. Clarification is requested, as mismatched addressing may affect billing, bond records, and notice validity.</span> <span class=chatlog__edited-timestamp title="Thursday, May 14, 2026 8:23 PM">(edited)</span></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1468909555713839165/Your_final_AGL_electricity_bill.pdf?ex=6a2dd361&amp;is=6a2c81e1&amp;hm=df16e672921153c5bb8dcc46322aae476be109e7250a094e0d0d794bbb075464&amp;"> Your_final_AGL_electricity_bill.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>400.94 KB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1468909556036931727/U1_7_Bakeri_Circuit.pdf?ex=6a2dd361&amp;is=6a2c81e1&amp;hm=25fbaa8ba5ed6011779711f55035ccd36d9a20cc19a2fd20303dd9599de9aade&amp;"> U1_7_Bakeri_Circuit.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>392.17 KB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1468909556326207681/7A_Bakeri_Cct_Stephen_-_Tenancy_Agreement.pdf?ex=