Image: 5.png (107.2 KB)" loading=lazy> </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1504394113347485776/6.png?ex=6a2e60b2&amp;is=6a2d0f32&amp;hm=40535d7a9d7478f1b119d4e2f1a622a53e990d71ed1bf243d3e61546c3401fd9&amp;"> <img class=chatlog__attachment-media src="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1504394113347485776/6.png?ex=6a2e60b2&amp;is=6a2d0f32&amp;hm=40535d7a9d7478f1b119d4e2f1a622a53e990d71ed1bf243d3e61546c3401fd9&amp;" alt="Image attachment" title="Image: 6.png (75.38 KB)" loading=lazy> </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1504394113762463864/7.png?ex=6a2e60b3&amp;is=6a2d0f33&amp;hm=e4f91d362bdf50f8c1f0b6a2b5bd4901569ebcaa8e0f311f8c0117fb26774f04&amp;"> <img class=chatlog__attachment-media src="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1504394113762463864/7.png?ex=6a2e60b3&amp;is=6a2d0f33&amp;hm=e4f91d362bdf50f8c1f0b6a2b5bd4901569ebcaa8e0f311f8c0117fb26774f04&amp;" alt="Image attachment" title="Image: 7.png (63.12 KB)" loading=lazy> </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1504394114274164797/8.png?ex=6a2e60b3&amp;is=6a2d0f33&amp;hm=99c998c537d6a1c96036d59038bc8deb8455654999c010c2b7109fd11d33d917&amp;"> <img class=chatlog__attachment-media src="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1504394114274164797/8.png?ex=6a2e60b3&amp;is=6a2d0f33&amp;hm=99c998c537d6a1c96036d59038bc8deb8455654999c010c2b7109fd11d33d917&amp;" alt="Image attachment" title="Image: 8.png (52.79 KB)" loading=lazy> </a></div></div></div></div></div>
<div class=chatlog__message-group><div id=chatlog__message-container-1504408400304541707 class=chatlog__message-container data-message-id=1504408400304541707><div class=chatlog__message><div class=chatlog__message-aside><img class=chatlog__avatar src=https://cdn.discordapp.com/embed/avatars/4.png alt=Avatar loading=lazy></div><div class=chatlog__message-primary><div class=chatlog__header><span class=chatlog__author title=dadventuressteve data-user-id=1264035953933156432>Veilocity</span> <span class=chatlog__timestamp title="Thursday, May 14, 2026 1:01 PM"><a href=#chatlog__message-container-1504408400304541707>5/14/2026 1:01 PM</a></span></div><div class="chatlog__content chatlog__markdown"><span class=chatlog__markdown-preserve><strong>Affidavit of Stephen Christopher Cooke – Variation Application and Single Expert Evidence Concerns — Cooke &amp; Cooke (NCC3896/2023) — 15/10/2024</strong>

This affidavit was filed by the Applicant Father in support of an application to vary orders made on 15 October 2024. The affidavit seeks permission for the Applicant to provide his affidavits and annexures directly to the Family Report Writer, including full medical records obtained under his right of access, which he states align with subpoenaed material.

The affidavit raises concerns regarding the flow of information to the Single Expert, noting that current orders place responsibility for provision of documents primarily with the Respondent’s solicitors, creating a risk of omission. It identifies discrepancies between subpoenas marked “awaiting production” and subpoenas that had in fact produced material but for which leave had not been granted.

The affidavit further addresses the drafting of the joint letter of instruction, noting it remained in draft form at the relevant time, and records disagreement regarding the exclusion of documents proposed by the Applicant, including property orders. It also seeks amendment of an existing order referencing child protection authorities, citing concern for potential emotional impact on the children, and seeks leave to exceed annexure limits to include material relating to housing stability and a psychological report concerning the children.

Extensive medical annexures are included, documenting ADHD diagnosis, prescribed treatment, absence of substance misuse concerns, and ongoing psychiatric management.

In the broader context of the proceedings, and when considered alongside the available correspondence, affidavits, court documents, expert materials, and procedural history, the matters raised in this affidavit reflect wider concerns regarding procedural fairness, information flow, and proportional assessment.

Observations arising from this material suggest that, at times, temporary circumstances may have been treated as indicative of permanent intent without later reassessment; interpretations may have been relied upon in the absence of verified findings; and cooperative conduct and procedural compliance were not consistently reflected in subsequent characterisations. Further, no clear corrective reassessment is evident where material facts changed, giving rise to concern that narrative momentum may, in some instances, have displaced neutral evaluation.

In addition, the material reflects a structural imbalance in which outcomes may be influenced by a party’s capacity to financially sustain participation. While decisions are not purchased and judicial intent is not impugned, the process may operate in practice as a pay-to-participate model, where access to representation, expert evidence, procedural navigation, and the ability to endure delay affect influence and leverage.

In such circumstances, financial capacity may function as a form of indirect control, exerting pressure toward compliance or settlement irrespective of substantive merit. Accordingly, the matters raised suggest a process in which procedural mechanisms and resource disparity may, in effect, outweigh considerations of fairness, proportionality, and individualised assessment.

These observations do not allege corruption, misconduct, or illegality, but rather reflect concern that lawful structures, when combined with unequal access to resources and constrained information flow, may operate coercively in effect, even in the absence of improper intent.</span></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1504408401105649714/Affidavit_P_NCC3896_2023_14193403.pdf?ex=6a2e6e01&amp;is=6a2d1c81&amp;hm=06428c9cf4b126465e9df10fc69bfff80038664a98eab86cc062fd01555c1bbb&amp;"> Affidavit_P_NCC3896_2023_14193403.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>5.14 MB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1504408401864556544/1.jpg?ex=6a2e6e01&amp;is=6a2d1c81&amp;hm=b1b17952fde49a7e48c2fb50de58819e7a9620c8d43dce3cae0290c53b3507fd&amp;"> <img class=chatlog__attachment-media src="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1504408401864556544/1.jpg?ex=6a2e6e01&amp;is=6a2d1c81&amp;hm=b1b17952fde49a7e48c2fb50de58819e7a9620c8d43dce3cae0290c53b3507fd&amp;" alt="Image attachment" title="Image: 1.jpg (4.54 MB)" loading=lazy> </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1504408402233659523/2.jpg?ex=6a2e6e01&amp;is=6a2d1c81&amp;hm=727ea70dfc6c48b254736af7a7dcc42d4dcd18dc100f6c6a875a7a3633298808&amp;"> <img class=chatlog__attachment-media src="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1504408402233659523/2.jpg?ex=6a2e6e01&amp;is=6a2d1c81&amp;hm=727ea70dfc6c48b254736af7a7dcc42d4dcd18dc100f6c6a875a7a3633298808&amp;" alt="Image attachment" title="Image: 2.jpg (194.71 KB)" loading=lazy> </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/