://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1504512861823565866/Gmail_-_Theyre_taking_all_the_assets..pdf?ex=6a2e268a&amp;is=6a2cd50a&amp;hm=4aee094d60577692bad174064c2df398c4fb463a08b8eccc908029522b792362&amp;"> Gmail_-_Theyre_taking_all_the_assets..pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>759.99 KB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><audio class=chatlog__attachment-media controls><source src="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1504512862117429438/Bought_Everything.wav?ex=6a2e268a&amp;is=6a2cd50a&amp;hm=babeeb1f3ff7c34fd4a89753f9e195b56e80484fcddc87f9d2d2151256eaae24&amp;" alt="Audio attachment" title="Audio: Bought_Everything.wav (1.32 MB)"></audio></div></div></div></div><div id=chatlog__message-container-1504513823728468098 class=chatlog__message-container data-message-id=1504513823728468098><div class=chatlog__message><div class=chatlog__message-aside><div class=chatlog__short-timestamp title="Thursday, May 14, 2026 8:00 PM">8:00 PM</div></div><div class=chatlog__message-primary><div class="chatlog__content chatlog__markdown"><span class=chatlog__markdown-preserve><strong>Mediation Arrangements Confirmation – Property-Focused Conference Before The Hon. Garry Foster — Cooke &amp; Cooke (NCC3896/2023) — 18/06/2024</strong>

The correspondence confirms arrangements for mediation listed for 18 June 2024 at 9:30am in Newcastle before The Hon. Garry Foster. Mr Foster acknowledges the matter and reiterates that mediation was requested in relation to property and parenting, noting the importance of resolving significant factual or valuation issues beforehand. He requests a collaboratively prepared Balance Sheet prior to mediation and confirms the process will be conducted on an evaluative basis. Anna Roberts responds to clarify that the mediation is intended to address property issues only, with parenting matters to be discussed only if property issues are resolved and time permits. She confirms her intention to cooperate in preparing the Balance Sheet and looks forward to working with the mediator. Mr Foster acknowledges this clarification.</span></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1504513823808295052/Re_MEDIATION_COOKE_18_JUNE_2024_0930AM_NEWCASTLE.pdf?ex=6a2e2770&amp;is=6a2cd5f0&amp;hm=091fa91ffa30f5959780c51ee44ade6688e041cbff447fdad334673bf31e9713&amp;"> Re_MEDIATION_COOKE_18_JUNE_2024_0930AM_NEWCASTLE.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>1.01 MB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1504513824122998925/Re_MEDIATION_COOKE_18_JUNE_2024_0930AM_NEWCASTLE.msg?ex=6a2e2770&amp;is=6a2cd5f0&amp;hm=a040efddc4d0d8b495e482a38c3e873e000fd94545641323463f9aaada6c91c7&amp;"> Re_MEDIATION_COOKE_18_JUNE_2024_0930AM_NEWCASTLE.msg </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>121 KB</div></div></div></div></div></div></div>
<div class=chatlog__message-group><div id=chatlog__message-container-1505608188727132291 class=chatlog__message-container data-message-id=1505608188727132291><div class=chatlog__message><div class=chatlog__message-aside><img class=chatlog__avatar src=https://cdn.discordapp.com/embed/avatars/4.png alt=Avatar loading=lazy></div><div class=chatlog__message-primary><div class=chatlog__header><span class=chatlog__author title=dadventuressteve data-user-id=1264035953933156432>Veilocity</span> <span class=chatlog__timestamp title="Sunday, May 17, 2026 8:29 PM"><a href=#chatlog__message-container-1505608188727132291>5/17/2026 8:29 PM</a></span></div><div class="chatlog__content chatlog__markdown"><span class=chatlog__markdown-preserve><strong> <img
    loading="lazy"
    class="chatlog__emoji "
    alt="⚖️"
    title="scales"
    src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/twitter/twemoji@latest/assets/svg/2696.svg"> Urgent Family Court Escalation &amp; Self-Representation Decision - 11/10/2024</strong>

This correspondence documents a critical escalation in family law proceedings involving subpoenas, parenting arrangements, and legal representation. The Applicant urgently seeks to secure medical and drug/alcohol testing records via subpoena to support his position, while simultaneously moving to amend his application toward a 50/50 parenting arrangement. The exchange highlights procedural complexities around subpoena approval, evidence submission, and expert report preparation, alongside growing concerns about delays, legal costs, and perceived inadequacies in representation. As pressures mount, the Applicant signals intent to self-represent, citing urgency, financial strain, and the need to directly control evidence and strategy to protect his parental relationship and ensure full consideration of relevant material before the Court.</span></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505608189109076098/Email_-_Urgent_Family_Court_Escalation__Self-Representation_Decision.pdf?ex=6a2e2e25&amp;is=6a2cdca5&amp;hm=c965051e7a5974e433e718f4da63b54a7423f8f62c5d2c6fd4506330e803b27e&amp;"> Email_-_Urgent_Family_Court_Escalation__Self-Representation_Decision.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>603.7 KB</div></div></div></div></div></div><div id=chatlog__message-container-1505608712151371776 class=chatlog__message-container data-message-id=1505608712151371776><div class=chatlog__message><div class=chatlog__message-aside><div class=chatlog__short-timestamp title="Sunday, May 17, 2026 8:31 PM">8:31 PM</div></div><div class=chatlog__message-primary><div class="chatlog__content chatlog__markdown"><span class=chatlog__markdown-preserve><strong><img
    loading="lazy"
    class="chatlog__emoji "
    alt="⚖️"
    title="scales"
    src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/twitter/twemoji@latest/assets/svg/2696.svg"> Final Parenting Orders Issued – Sole Custody, No Contact &amp; Cost Orders - 17/11/2025</strong>

This correspondence formally serves sealed Final Orders issued by the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia, determining the Cooke &amp; Cooke matter on a default basis without the Applicant’s appearance. The Orders grant the Respondent Mother sole parental responsibility, sole decision-making authority, and exclusive care of the children, while removing all time and communication rights from the Applicant Father. The Orders further impose strict injunctive restraints preventing proximity or contact, and authorise unilateral passport control and international travel by the Mother. In addition, significant financial obligations are imposed, including fixed contributions to the Independent Children’s Lawyer and legal costs payable to the Respondent. The correspondence also provides payment instructions and confirms enforcement expectations arising from the sealed Orders.</span></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505608712298041375/Final_Orders_sealed_17.11.25.pdf?ex=6a2e2ea1&amp;is=6a2cdd21&amp;hm=98473d0449b0719f08fb0bd55db3e4a4a9354ce7d16e111bc0e3bc8daf70c0b2&amp;"> Final_Orders_sealed_17.11.25.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>595.8 KB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505608712612479136/Email_-_Final_Parenting_Orders_Issued_Sole_Custody_No_Contact__Cost_Orders_-_17112025.pdf?ex=6a2e2ea1&amp;is=6a2cdd21&amp;hm=5c1d4655039f86912d665259a1f91578665a7b570f57f582018d893b9f6971b3&amp;"> Email_-_Final_Parenting_Orders_Issued_Sole_Custody_No_Contact__Cost_Orders_-_17112025.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>715.07 KB</div></div></div></div></div></div></div>
<div class=chatlog__message-group><div id=chatlog__message-container-1505610989024841759 class=chatlog__message-container data-message-id=1505610989024841759><div class=chatlog__message><div class=chatlog__message-aside><img class=chatlog__avatar src=https://cdn.discordapp.com/embed/avatars/4.png alt=Avatar loading=lazy></div><div class=chatlog__message-primary><div class=chatlog__header><span class=chatlog__author title=dadventuressteve data-user-id=1264035953933156432>Veilocity</span> <span class=chatlog__timestamp title="Sunday, May 17, 2026 8:40 PM"><a href=#chatlog__message-container-1505610989024841759>5/17/2026 8:40 PM</a></span></div><div class="chatlog__content chatlog__markdown"><span class=chatlog__markdown-preserve><strong>Cooke &amp; Cooke (NCC3896/2023) – Consolidated Case Summary: Evidence, Proceedings, and Final Determination</strong>

This matter concerns parenting proceedings between Stephen Christopher Cooke (Applicant Father) and Heather Anne Cooke (Respondent Mother), culminating in final orders issued on 17 November 2025 by the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia.

Prior to trial, the Respondent’s legal representatives formally served the Court and parties with a comprehensive evidentiary package, including a primary affidavit, supporting affidavit, exhibit index (“HC”), and costs notice. The affidavit sets out a detailed narrative of the relationship, caregiving roles, and post-separation events, including allegations relating to parenting capacity, communication difficulties, and incidents involving the children. The exhibit index links over 30 categories of supporting material—medical records, communications, school interactions, legal correspondence, and third-party evidence—directly to specific affidavit claims. A supplementary affidavit formalises the collection of social media content attributed to the Applicant for evidentiary use.

The materials also document events in March 2025, after which the children ceased spending time with the Applicant, alongside references to police welfare checks, mental health intervention, and the Applicant’s subsequent absence and international travel. A costs notice filed prior to trial outlines legal expenditure exceeding $186,000, with projected total costs surpassing $236,000.

Email correspondence confirms procedural compliance, including service of affidavits, exhibits, and costs documentation, and coordination with the Independent Children’s Lawyer regarding fees and trial preparation.

The proceedings were ultimately determined on a default basis in the absence of the Applicant. Final orders granted the Respondent sole parental responsibility, exclusive care of the children, and removed all time and communication between the children and the Applicant. Additional orders imposed injunctive restraints limiting proximity and contact, authorised unilateral decision-making including international travel, and required the Applicant to contribute to legal and Independent Children’s Lawyer costs.

Collectively, the material reflects a structured evidentiary and procedural progression from pre-trial disclosure through to final determination, with the Court’s orders aligning with the Respondent’s presented position and supporting documentation.</span></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505610989326962808/Email_-_Cooke__Cooke_NCC38962023_Consolidated_Case_Summary_Evidence_Proceedings_and_Final_Determination.pdf?ex=6a2e30c0&amp;is=6a2cdf40&amp;hm=97e0a7ba475b253fe1138209e3133cf20e30a1163b3058d565817d87a961164e&amp;"> Email_-_Cooke__Cooke_NCC38962023_Consolidated_Case_Summary_Evidence_Proceedings_and_Final_Determination.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>386.94 KB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505610989733806162/Affidavit_of_Heather_Anne_Cooke_sealed_20_October_2025.pdf?ex=6a2e30c0&amp;is=6a2cdf40&amp;hm=b9d5fd0ef580b3db2d1d30eaf902e093ecc5a9cf11945d65d9950496bbb746d9&amp;"> Affidavit_of_Heather_Anne_Cooke_sealed_20_October_2025.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>3.64 MB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505610989993726083/Affidavit_of_Taylor_Jordain_Toni_sealed_20_October_2025.pdf?ex=6a2e30c0&amp;is=6a2cdf40&amp;hm=d83ba4d744dee4bb69e200851411e0098c03a8fdfb4cc8bfe773a9fb88de16ee&amp;"> Affidavit_of_Taylor_Jordain_Toni_sealed_20_October_2025.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>640.26 KB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505610990354567248/Exhibits_to_Affidavit_of_Heather_Anne_Cooke_sealed_20_October_2025.pdf?ex=6a2e30c1&amp;is=6a2cdf41&amp;hm=0e25fe4822c1396b650cd99f98a81b067ac076b5163bd21177bbb73015adf5a7&amp;"> Exhibits_to_Affidavit_of_Heather_Anne_Cooke_sealed_20_October_2025.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>8.86 MB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505610990648037547/Costs_Notice_sealed_10.11.25.pdf?ex=6a2e30c1&amp;is=6a2cdf41&amp;hm=28f4ec2e8191ef44ff6088c0558dda1127aff5cdaae9f169dfc3def063bc4e93&amp;"> Costs_Notice_sealed_10.11.25.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>203.91 KB</div></div></div></div></div></div><div id=chatlog__message-container-1505611754888105996 class=chatlog__message-container data-message-id=1505611754888105996><div class=chatlog__message><div class=chatlog__message-aside><div class=chatlog__short-timestamp title="Sunday, May 17, 2026 8:43 PM">8:43 PM</div></div><div class=chatlog__message-primary><div class="chatlog__content chatlog__markdown"><span class=chatlog__markdown-preserve><strong>Trial Directions Orders – Evidence Control, Tender Bundle Restrictions &amp; Cross-Examination Limits - 07/04/2025</strong>

These Trial Directions Orders, made by His Honour Judge Betts, establish the procedural framework for the Cooke &amp; Cooke proceedings leading to the final hearing in November 2025. The Orders set strict requirements for the filing, service, and reliance upon evidence, including deadlines for affidavits, witness material, and outline of case documents. They govern the creation and submission of Tender Bundles, requiring that evidentiary material be compiled, indexed, and provided directly to the Court, while restricting direct access to subpoenaed material to legal representatives only. Provision is made for self-represented parties to view such material at the Registry, but not to possess it.

Importantly, the Orders prohibit the parties from personally cross-examining each other, invoking protections associated with allegations of family violence. They also limit the ability to introduce new material after expert reports, reinforce strict compliance requirements for admissibility of evidence, and formalise cost disclosure obligations prior to trial. Collectively, these directions define the evidentiary boundaries, proce</span></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505611755097817212/Orders_sealed_07.04.25_final_hearing.pdf?ex=6a2e3177&amp;is=6a2cdff7&amp;hm=ec8a00636eb58f04b41e5bb434b0326306238db5ec4cf88942fefd12e5ec30c0&amp;"> Orders_sealed_07.04.25_final_hearing.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>512.77 KB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505611755420647465/Email_-_Trial_Directions_Orders_Evidence_Control_Tender_Bundle_Restrictions__Cross-Examination_Limits_07042025.pdf?ex=6a2e3177&amp;is=6a2cdff7&amp;hm=03e2b773b2cdfde57dbfa02d76cd5909589983ee22e6af95887aeab03cfa7c93&amp;"> Email_-_Trial_Directions_Orders_Evidence_Control_Tender_Bundle_Restrictions__Cross-Examination_Limits_07042025.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>378.41 KB</div></div></div></div></div></div><div id=chatlog__message-container-1505612868274487467 class=chatlog__message-container data-message-id=1505612868274487467><div class=chatlog__message><div class=chatlog__message-aside><div class=chatlog__short-timestamp title="Sunday, May 17, 2026 8:48 PM">8:48 PM</div></div><div class=chatlog__message-primary><div class="chatlog__content chatlog__markdown"><span class=chatlog__markdown-preserve><strong><img
    loading="lazy"
    class="chatlog__emoji "
    alt="⚖️"
    title="scales"
    src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/twitter/twemoji@latest/assets/svg/2696.svg"> Remote Participation Sought, Absence Recorded &amp; Procedural Barrier Imposed – Pre-Trial Communication and Orders - 28/10/2025 – 03/11/2025</strong>

This sequence of correspondence and Orders documents the Applicant Father’s confirmed intention to participate in the final hearing and the procedural developments that followed immediately prior to trial. On 28 October 2025, the Applicant formally notified the Court and all parties of his intention to fully participate and requested remote attendance due to safety concerns and his presence overseas. The Court responded by listing the matter for 3 November 2025 to consider this request and granted leave for all parties to appear by video for that interim listing.

In parallel, the Independent Children’s Lawyer raised uncertainty regarding the Applicant’s participation and noted that trial materials had not yet been filed. The Applicant subsequently reiterated his commitment, explained technical issues affecting his ability to attend the interim listing, and confirmed ongoing efforts to comply with filing requirements, including preparation of his affidavit and trial materials.

The Orders made on 3 November 2025 record the Applicant’s non-appearance at that listing and the absence of filed trial material at that time, while also acknowledging his earlier communication requesting remote attendance. The Court maintained the final hearing dates but imposed a formal requirement that any request to appear by video must be made through the appropriate application process before it would be considered.

Taken together, the email exchange and Orders demonstrate a sequence in which the Applicant actively communicated his intention to participate and sought remote access, but encountered procedural requirements and technical barriers that impacted his ability to attend the interim listing and finalise compliance within the required timeframe.</span></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505612868551184515/Email_-_Remote_Participation_Sought_Absence_Recorded__Procedural_Barrier_Imposed.pdf?ex=6a2e3280&amp;is=6a2ce100&amp;hm=bf18780de18e2fc7f7931985458bc0e8a521d2e0f45ea244459a178903d578ca&amp;"> Email_-_Remote_Participation_Sought_Absence_Recorded__Procedural_Barrier_Imposed.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>1.1 MB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505612868802838741/Stephen_Cooke_Affidavit_Nov_4_2025.pdf?ex=6a2e3280&amp;is=6a2ce100&amp;hm=2167effe64c258caf4ba59572dbe3886fb312f884b4b6aa1c331d87d20493fac&amp;"> Stephen_Cooke_Affidavit_Nov_4_2025.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>7.76 MB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505612869134450788/Cooke_Order_3_November_2025.pdf?ex=6a2e3280&amp;is=6a2ce100&amp;hm=3cd7de4148f1fa98c78dbb672eda040dbe8946d5e3cb1b48f3ccc9fc7ec32a60&amp;"> Cooke_Order_3_November_2025.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>286.08 KB</div></div></div></div></div></div></div>
<div class=chatlog__message-group><div id=chatlog__message-container-1505615187158372473 class=chatlog__message-container data-message-id=1505615187158372473><div class=chatlog__message><div class=chatlog__message-aside><img class=chatlog__avatar src=https://cdn.discordapp.com/embed/avatars/4.png alt=Avatar loading=lazy></div><div class=chatlog__message-primary><div class=chatlog__header><span class=chatlog__author title=dadventuressteve data-user-id=1264035953933156432>Veilocity</span> <span class=chatlog__timestamp title="Sunday, May 17, 2026 8:57 PM"><a href=#chatlog__message-container-1505615187158372473>5/17/2026 8:57 PM</a></span></div><div class="chatlog__content chatlog__markdown"><span class=chatlog__markdown-preserve><strong>Expert Engagement Terms vs Court Orders – Updating Material Permitted in Contract but Prohibited by Trial Directions (31/10/2025 – 04/11/2025)</strong>

This correspondence and accompanying attachments document the confirmed booking of a Court-appointed expert, Drew Cowen, for cross-examination on 19 November 2025, alongside the governing Terms of Engagement issued by the expert’s office. The Terms explicitly allow for the submission of up to 200 pages of jointly agreed “updating materials” as part of preparation for cross-examination, with additional material permitted subject to fee structures and strict upload requirements.

However, in direct response, the Respondent’s legal representatives invoked Trial Directions Orders dated 7 April 2025, which expressly prohibit parties from providing the Single Expert with any documents post-dating the most recent report unless otherwise ordered. This position was consented to by the Independent Children’s Lawyer and communicated back to the expert’s office.

The result is a clear procedural conflict: the expert’s engagement framework anticipates and accommodates updated evidentiary input, while the Court Orders restrict any such updates. Consequently, the expert proceeded to cross-examination without receiving updated materials, limiting the scope of review to previously filed evidence and reinforcing the evidentiary constraints imposed prior to trial.</span></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505615187548573929/Email_-_Expert_Engagement_Terms_vs_Court_Orders.pdf?ex=6a2e34a9&amp;is=6a2ce329&amp;hm=b3ef511c21e53c5a250530697b7469360fd8300a6582bf43e4e012201b2bce57&amp;"> Email_-_Expert_Engagement_Terms_vs_Court_Orders.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>1.07 MB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505615188093567047/Orders_sealed_07.04.25_final_hearing.pdf?ex=6a2e34a9&amp;is=6a2ce329&amp;hm=ab2202036a9eff2efb0d9ce014a23911afc497e330f34216b731656b87b0bbcc&amp;"> Orders_sealed_07.04.25_final_hearing.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>7.98 MB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505615188685230281/Index_Template.docx?ex=6a2e34a9&amp;is=6a2ce329&amp;hm=d081ef526f72ff4d8bd5a198f1bdb478feb829111e92ec84d69501ee108cbac1&amp;"> Index_Template.docx </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>154.33 KB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505615189075034283/Terms_of_Engagement_-_all_reports_21.6.25.pdf?ex=6a2e34aa&amp;is=6a2ce32a&amp;hm=a12062f71214863f83e39f5fac35a367c724d442a451c7bbadfe7c2b0149bfac&amp;"> Terms_of_Engagement_-_all_reports_21.6.25.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>325.96 KB</div></div></div></div></div></div><div id=chatlog__message-container-1505616404957757560 class=chatlog__message-container data-message-id=1505616404957757560><div class=chatlog__message><div class=chatlog__message-aside><div class=chatlog__short-timestamp title="Sunday, May 17, 2026 9:02 PM">9:02 PM</div></div><div class=chatlog__message-primary><div class="chatlog__content chatlog__markdown"><span class=chatlog__markdown-preserve><strong>Parenting Variation Application &amp; Supporting Affidavit – Evidence of Capacity, Procedural Concerns &amp; Information Flow Issues - 07/11/2024</strong>

This material comprises the Applicant Father’s Application in a Proceeding and supporting Affidavit filed on 7 November 2024 in the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia. Together, these documents formally seek variation of prior orders and establish the evidentiary foundation for the Applicant’s parenting position.

The affidavit outlines the Applicant’s request to provide full medical records and supporting annexures directly to the Family Report Writer, asserting that these materials demonstrate stable mental health, ongoing treatment compliance, and capacity to meet parental responsibilities.

A central issue raised is the control and asymmetry of information flow. The Applicant expresses concern that responsibility for providing material to the Single Expert rests primarily with the Respondent’s legal team, creating risk of omission or imbalance. This concern is reinforced by discrepancies identified in subpoena handling—where certain subpoenaed materials were referenced despite being “awaiting production,” while other available materials had not been granted leave for use.

The affidavit further documents disputes regarding the scope of relevant evidence, including the exclusion of property settlement orders (despite their relevance to financial stability), and challenges in collaborative drafting of the joint letter of instruction to the expert. It also seeks amendment of an order referencing child protection authorities, citing concern for potential emotional harm to the children.

Additional annexures are relied upon to demonstrate housing stability, parenting environment, and concerns regarding the impact of a child’s ADHD medication on emotional development.

Taken together, the application and affidavit establish (1) active procedural engagement by the Applicant, (2) a clear attempt to place full evidentiary material before the expert, and (3) early identification of concerns regarding fairness, completeness, and control of information within the expert report process.</span></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505616405406683297/Email_-_Parenting_Variation_Application__Supporting_Affidavit.pdf?ex=6a2e35cc&amp;is=6a2ce44c&amp;hm=8c46f28fa1e278cd6e3acb65d494597475663c97e65854bc9bfacbd4d8909381&amp;"> Email_-_Parenting_Variation_Application__Supporting_Affidavit.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>612.9 KB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505616405813395476/Application_P_NCC3896_2023_14193402.pdf?ex=6a2e35cc&amp;is=6a2ce44c&amp;hm=5f3545ebbfac2156d072011a05053dcbe151422e2bdf94b181f7754ae6a2eb94&amp;"> Application_P_NCC3896_2023_14193402.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>1.58 MB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505616406182629508/Affidavit_P_NCC3896_2023_14193403.pdf?ex=6a2e35cc&amp;is=6a2ce44c&amp;hm=999777390df767364998d9940b91d6ef65ad00d485eb0dc6fd8362dc97510b61&amp;"> Affidavit_P_NCC3896_2023_14193403.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>12 MB</div></div></div></div></div></div><div id=chatlog__message-container-1505617658580566148 class=chatlog__message-container data-message-id=1505617658580566148><div class=chatlog__message><div class=chatlog__message-aside><div class=chatlog__short-timestamp title="Sunday, May 17, 2026 9:07 PM">9:07 PM</div></div><div class=chatlog__message-primary><div class="chatlog__content chatlog__markdown"><span class=chatlog__markdown-preserve><strong>Child Impact Assessment Coordination &amp; Communication Record – OurFamilyWizard Exchange - 23/12/2024</strong>

This OurFamilyWizard message exchange documents communication between the parties regarding the scheduling and coordination of the children’s Child Impact Assessment, set for 27 February 2025 in Sydney.

The Respondent Mother initially advised that the assessment had been scheduled and that she would transport the children to Sydney, with the Applicant Father to return them to Newcastle. The Applicant subsequently requested confirmation details, including the exact time and formal correspondence from The Relationspace, noting he had not received any direct communication regarding the appointment.

The Respondent replied that the correspondence had been sent via email and suggested checking spam, offering to resend if required. The exchange concludes with the Applicant confirming receipt.

This communication reflects (1) notification of a significant court-ordered assessment, (2) the Applicant’s proactive request for full and direct information, and (3) reliance on indirect transmission of key procedural details rather than direct service from the expert provider.</span></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505617659218104422/Email_Child_Impact_Assessment_Coordination__Communication_Record_23-12-2024.pdf?ex=6a2e36f6&amp;is=6a2ce576&amp;hm=0b442106da539c037a3de949e64db500fdab800a0670345666e9dced954bd069&amp;"> Email_Child_Impact_Assessment_Coordination__Communication_Record_23-12-2024.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>1.45 MB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505617659595587635/JLI_SER_Cooke_DC.pdf?ex=6a2e36f7&amp;is=6a2ce577&amp;hm=f69fd435b21457a906b16d28293407de5e0a420ca49d23fc5ba663e901bc7a72&amp;"> JLI_SER_Cooke_DC.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>931.33 KB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505617660103360652/Sydney_Confirmation_OFW_Messages_Report_2025-01-15_01-54-44.pdf?ex=6a2e36f7&amp;is=6a2ce577&amp;hm=18d6f1d0fea5682e9838bce2411bde732a7543e8cf8d957fd081cf3818736e5e&amp;"> Sydney_Confirmation_OFW_Messages_Report_2025-01-15_01-54-44.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>69.69 KB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505617660572995716/15-Oct-2024_-_Single_Expert_1400_Mention_Judicial_Registrar_Furner_Continuing_To_Different_Sitting_Type.pdf?ex=6a2e36f7&amp;is=6a2ce577&amp;hm=12765a48e091a0eb853a609a4fe6db876bffbe8529ae69756720dd14f6a7403c&amp;"> 15-Oct-2024_-_Single_Expert_1400_Mention_Judicial_Registrar_Furner_Continuing_To_Different_Sitting_Type.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>525.45 KB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505617660946284634/Terms_of_Engagement_-_all_reports.pdf?ex=6a2e36f7&amp;is=6a2ce577&amp;hm=1c27681f2d755fa96801455fe8166cfade5d7d708d586ca23a68828868c2b554&amp;"> Terms_of_Engagement_-_all_reports.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>227.79 KB</div></div></div></div></div></div><div id=chatlog__message-container-1505618807396368404 class=chatlog__message-container data-message-id=1505618807396368404><div class=chatlog__message><div class=chatlog__message-aside><div class=chatlog__short-timestamp title="Sunday, May 17, 2026 9:11 PM">9:11 PM</div></div><div class=chatlog__message-primary><div class="chatlog__content chatlog__markdown"><span class=chatlog__markdown-preserve><strong>Cooke &amp; Cooke Correspondence &amp; Evidence Set – Property Settlement, Parenting Proceedings &amp; Expert Process - 23/09/2024</strong>

These documents collectively relate to family law proceedings between Stephen Christopher Cooke (Applicant Father) and Heather Anne Cooke (Respondent Mother), covering both property settlement and parenting matters within the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia.

The material spans multiple stages of the proceedings, including:

Property settlement execution, involving distribution of sale proceeds held in trust, disputes regarding timing of payment, and allocation of funds such as styling cost refunds.
Parenting proceedings, including applications filed by the Applicant seeking parenting orders and supporting affidavit material addressing parenting capacity, medical context, and proposed care arrangements.
Expert (Family Report) process, involving coordination of a Single Expert, preparation of a joint letter of instruction, submission of indexed materials, and disputes over what evidence could be provided to the expert.
Procedural communications, including emails between parties, lawyers, and the Court regarding compliance with orders, deadlines, and participation in hearings.

The documents also reflect ongoing issues around timing, communication, and control of information, including delays in fund distribution, clarification of evidence to be considered by the expert, and coordination of key procedural steps.

Overall, the material forms a chronological record of how financial matters were finalised and how parenting issues progressed through evidence gathering, expert involvement, and Court-managed procedures.</span> <span class=chatlog__edited-timestamp title="Sunday, May 17, 2026 9:11 PM">(edited)</span></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505618807513940018/Emails_re_overpaid_styling_costs_1.pdf?ex=6a2e3808&amp;is=6a2ce688&amp;hm=71fc73e63d3b4eaef940eb33d1f4a1897e838dc297cce63343d5702a641e0496&amp;"> Emails_re_overpaid_styling_costs_1.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>515.4 KB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505618807966666934/Email_Cooke__Cooke_Correspondence__Evidence_Set_Property_Settlement_Parenting_Proceedings__Expert_Process_23-09-2024.pdf?ex=6a2e3808&amp;is=6a2ce688&amp;hm=7c79f6202425752fbb3546df47df946fc9497e61dfcd6788d525682ccfe606bf&amp;"> Email_Cooke__Cooke_Correspondence__Evidence_Set_Property_Settlement_Parenting_Proceedings__Expert_Process_23-09-2024.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>597.58 KB</div></div></div></div></div></div><div id=chatlog__message-container-1505619659528077485 class=chatlog__message-container data-message-id=1505619659528077485><div class=chatlog__message><div class=chatlog__message-aside><div class=chatlog__short-timestamp title="Sunday, May 17, 2026 9:14 PM">9:14 PM</div></div><div class=chatlog__message-primary><div class="chatlog__content chatlog__markdown"><span class=chatlog__markdown-preserve><strong>Application to Limit Costs &amp; Property Settlement Finalisation – Strategic Push to Conclude Proceedings - 10/09/2024</strong>

This correspondence documents the Applicant Father’s concerns regarding escalating legal costs and his request to pursue an application to limit costs within the Cooke &amp; Cooke proceedings. The Applicant identifies multiple factors contributing to increased expenses, including ongoing legal correspondence, repeated mediation attempts, disputed parenting narratives being introduced into property matters, and alleged delays in financial disclosure. He asserts that these actions have resulted in significant financial strain, including substantial legal fees incurred in responding to allegations and procedural developments.

In parallel, communication between legal representatives confirms that the parties had reached agreement in principle to resolve the property settlement, with proposed Consent Orders submitted to the Court for approval. The settlement outlines the division of assets and liabilities, resulting in an approximate 57/43 split (non-superannuation) in favour of the Applicant and near-equal division when superannuation is included.

The Applicant’s legal representative advises that the most cost-effective course is to finalise the property settlement immediately and proceed with parenting matters separately, rather than pursuing further applications or prolonging dispute resolution processes. The correspondence also highlights a strategic approach to resolving property issues without conceding to disputed parenting allegations, preserving the distinction between financial settlement and parenting proceedings.

Overall, these documents reflect (1) a clear effort by the Applicant to contain legal costs and bring finality to financial matters, (2) formal progression toward property settlement through Consent Orders, and (3) ongoing tension regarding the overlap of parenting narratives within financial negotiations.</span></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505619659787862066/Email_-_Application_to_Limit_Costs__Property_Settlement_Finalisation.pdf?ex=6a2e38d3&amp;is=6a2ce753&amp;hm=636e480128696941cf47800217e70a24f1fec71a1e50c8b43dc9a7d82b57be7c&amp;"> Email_-_Application_to_Limit_Costs__Property_Settlement_Finalisation.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>694.17 KB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505619660119474257/4924_Letter_to_ct_drafted_by_RFL.pdf?ex=6a2e38d4&amp;is=6a2ce754&amp;hm=d0078f31d9fe2fb35f387ff535351a2537083348e191bae3389dd3d62eb636d1&amp;"> 4924_Letter_to_ct_drafted_by_RFL.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>343.59 KB</div></div></div></div></div></div></div>
<div class=chatlog__message-group><div id=chatlog__message-container-1505622164068372641 class=chatlog__message-container data-message-id=1505622164068372641><div class=chatlog__message><div class=chatlog__message-aside><img class=chatlog__avatar src=https://cdn.discordapp.com/embed/avatars/4.png alt=Avatar loading=lazy></div><div class=chatlog__message-primary><div class=chatlog__header><span class=chatlog__author title=dadventuressteve data-user-id=1264035953933156432>Veilocity</span> <span class=chatlog__timestamp title="Sunday, May 17, 2026 9:24 PM"><a href=#chatlog__message-container-1505622164068372641>5/17/2026 9:24 PM</a></span></div><div class="chatlog__content chatlog__markdown"><span class=chatlog__markdown-preserve><strong>Personal Crisis, Relocation &amp; Ongoing Proceedings – Remote Participation, Financial Disruption and Family Communication 31/01/2026</strong>

This correspondence documents a significant personal and legal turning point in April 2025, where the Applicant Father outlines circumstances surrounding involuntary hospitalisation under the Mental Health Act, subsequent relocation to Thailand, and resulting impacts on his ability to participate in ongoing family law proceedings. The material includes communication to the Court requesting continued remote participation due to safety and wellbeing concerns, alongside complaints to financial institutions and a hospital regarding restricted access to funds and reimbursement of monies taken during admission. Concurrently, a family member provides contextual information from discussions with medical staff, indicating the detention was precautionary and treatment temporary. The documents also reflect the Applicant’s concern for his children, acknowledgment of ongoing custody proceedings, and the broader impact of financial disruption and geographic separation on his capacity to engage in the matter.</span></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505622164114767952/Email_Personal_Crisis_Relocation__Ongoing_Proceedings.pdf?ex=6a2e3b29&amp;is=6a2ce9a9&amp;hm=e71b6ff39e80f1712fe029ac2d953a333e56cfdc43b6aab7348ea74adbbb918b&amp;"> Email_Personal_Crisis_Relocation__Ongoing_Proceedings.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>923.35 KB</div></div></div></div></div></div></div>
<div class=chatlog__message-group><div id=chatlog__message-container-1505624265280716915 class=chatlog__message-container data-message-id=1505624265280716915><div class=chatlog__message><div class=chatlog__message-aside><img class=chatlog__avatar src=https://cdn.discordapp.com/embed/avatars/4.png alt=Avatar loading=lazy></div><div class=chatlog__message-primary><div class=chatlog__header><span class=chatlog__author title=dadventuressteve data-user-id=1264035953933156432>Veilocity</span> <span class=chatlog__timestamp title="Sunday, May 17, 2026 9:33 PM"><a href=#chatlog__message-container-1505624265280716915>5/17/2026 9:33 PM</a></span></div><div class="chatlog__content chatlog__markdown"><span class=chatlog__markdown-preserve><strong><img
