    src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/twitter/twemoji@latest/assets/svg/1f4c8.svg"> 17/05/2026</strong>

The documents collectively outline escalating legal costs in family law proceedings between Stephen Cooke (Applicant) and Heather Cooke (Respondent) under file NCC3896/2023. Early 2024 notices show initial costs around $29k–$98k for the Applicant and ~$15k for the Respondent, with projected totals ranging $100k–$145k for a final hearing . By mid-2024, Applicant costs significantly increased, including ~$127k with Clarity Lawyers and growing Ramsdens fees, with anticipated total future costs exceeding $115k–$121k for trial stages . Respondent costs similarly escalated, reaching ~$107k by July and projected totals near $190k+ . By late 2024, Respondent costs rose to ~$145k actual and ~$219k projected , while Applicant totals reached ~$205k billed/unbilled with further ~$77k anticipated . Funding sources include income, savings, litigation finance, and trust funds from property sale. Overall, both parties face substantial, compounding legal expenses driven by ongoing hearings, expert reports, and preparation for a multi-day final trial.</span></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505624265808941136/08-07-2024_-_SC_-_Costs_Notice_Ramsden_Family_Law.pdf?ex=6a2e3d1e&amp;is=6a2ceb9e&amp;hm=7a92367e5ca1e6963bbbbf1ab81c1d9824cd3bcef2ccc6da9547ba6ecc628d4f&amp;"> 08-07-2024_-_SC_-_Costs_Notice_Ramsden_Family_Law.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>52.64 KB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1505624266153132262/09-Jul-2024_1046_Costs_Notice_Delaney_Roberts_Family_Lawyers.pdf?ex=6a2e3d1e&amp;