<div class=chatlog__message-group><div id=chatlog__message-container-1508027480131375175 class=chatlog__message-container data-message-id=1508027480131375175><div class=chatlog__message><div class=chatlog__message-aside><img class=chatlog__avatar src=https://cdn.discordapp.com/embed/avatars/4.png alt=Avatar loading=lazy></div><div class=chatlog__message-primary><div class=chatlog__header><span class=chatlog__author title=dadventuressteve data-user-id=1264035953933156432>Veilocity</span> <span class=chatlog__timestamp title="Sunday, May 24, 2026 12:42 PM"><a href=#chatlog__message-container-1508027480131375175>5/24/2026 12:42 PM</a></span></div><div class="chatlog__content chatlog__markdown"><span class=chatlog__markdown-preserve><strong>Forensic Accounting Concerns &amp; Historical Property Transactions – Family Law Proceedings - 08/05/2024</strong>

This correspondence outlines Stephen Cooke’s efforts to engage a forensic accountant in preparation for ongoing family law property proceedings and mediation. The material raises concerns regarding transparency, disclosure, asset tracing, mortgage increases, rental income, foreign assets, and the movement of substantial funds during the marriage. Stephen sought independent forensic review of financial records, including questions surrounding approximately $400,000 removed from a joint account prior to separation, mortgage redraws, rental income from investment properties, and proceeds from the sale of a South Brisbane property previously owned by Heather Anne Finn. Supporting conveyancing documents, title searches, contracts, disclosure statements, and legal correspondence relating to the 2012 sale of Unit 28, 9–11 Manning Street, South Brisbane were attached to establish historical financial context and ownership records. Concerns were also expressed regarding delayed disclosure from the opposing side prior to mediation, creating pressure and limiting adequate review time. The material reflects a broader attempt to obtain accountability, clarity, and independent verification of financial matters central to the property settlement process.</span></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1508027480685019276/EMAIL_-_Forensic_Accounting_Concerns__Historical_Property_Transactions.pdf?ex=6a2e6989&amp;is=6a2d1809&amp;hm=92ba1ac808b9f475b458f3913de32f3bbd6bfe2a2f49cc7beee6c76e33cdb74d&amp;"> EMAIL_-_Forensic_Accounting_Concerns__Historical_Property_Transactions.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>396.96 KB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-