<div class=chatlog__message-group><div id=chatlog__message-container-1508041484589600900 class=chatlog__message-container data-message-id=1508041484589600900><div class=chatlog__message><div class=chatlog__message-aside><img class=chatlog__avatar src=https://cdn.discordapp.com/embed/avatars/4.png alt=Avatar loading=lazy></div><div class=chatlog__message-primary><div class=chatlog__header><span class=chatlog__author title=dadventuressteve data-user-id=1264035953933156432>Veilocity</span> <span class=chatlog__timestamp title="Sunday, May 24, 2026 1:38 PM"><a href=#chatlog__message-container-1508041484589600900>5/24/2026 1:38 PM</a></span></div><div class="chatlog__content chatlog__markdown"><span class=chatlog__markdown-preserve><strong>Proposed Consent Orders &amp; Final Property Settlement Negotiations – Cooke vs Cooke 03/09/2024</strong>

This material concerns negotiations surrounding proposed Consent Orders intended to finalise the property settlement in the Cooke family law proceedings during September 2024. The documents include communications between Stephen Cooke, his solicitor Matthew Shepherd of Ramsden Family Law, and the Court regarding division of assets, liabilities, superannuation, interim property distributions, parenting contributions, and disputes surrounding joint funds, spousal maintenance, and the sale of the former matrimonial home.

With hindsight, the material also appears to contradict broader assertions made elsewhere regarding Stephen Cooke’s capability and stability. Despite years outside the workforce while operating primarily in a homemaker and parenting role, the records simultaneously demonstrate retraining, pursuit of education, transition into the IT sector, and movement toward full-time paid employment earning a fair income.

Stephen’s ability to fully stabilise long-term IT employment was ultimately disrupted by escalating safety concerns, reputational destruction, institutional pressure, and coercive legal and psychological scrutiny which, in practical effect, forced him to flee the country before stability could be re-established.

The only debt specifically identified at the commencement of cohabitation was a credit card debt resolved through a loan from Stephen Cooke’s parents. With hindsight, Stephen increasingly viewed the experience as involving the progressive transfer of dependency and authority over his life between systems rather than genuine support toward autonomy and independence — first through the marital structure, and later through legal, institutional, mental health, parental, and state systems. The cumulative effect described is one of profound destabilisation, loss of autonomy, and erosion of personal agency during attempts to rebuild financial independence and personal stability.</span></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1508041484677677107/EMAIL_-_Proposed_Consent_Orders__Final_Property_Settlement_Negotiations.pdf?ex=6a2dcdd4&amp;is=6a2c7c54&amp;hm=3dfa755a82e66c1312612c43701096452188cf51795fc68419593ee58ef6b379&amp;"> EMAIL_-_Proposed_Consent_Orders__Final_Property_Settlement_Negotiations.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>397.93 KB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1508041484971020379/02.09.24_Joint_Letter_to_the_Court_signed_by_the_Respondent.pdf?ex=6a2dcdd4&amp;is=6a2c7c54&amp;hm=336546b6ae7e372ca7073539dc05e19e43d3f35502e34fa153a92cee2e805b53&amp;"> 02.09.24_Joint_Letter_to_the_Court_signed_by_the_Respondent.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>505.63 KB</div></div></div></div></div></div></div>
<div class=chatlog__message-group><div id=chatlog__message-container-1508046001162813471 class=chatlog__message-container data-message-id=1508046001162813471><div class=chatlog__message><div class=chatlog__message-aside><img class=chatlog__avatar src=https://cdn.discordapp.com/embed/avatars/4.png alt=Avatar loading=lazy></div><div class=chatlog__message-primary><div class=chatlog__header><span class=chatlog__author title=dadventuressteve data-user-id=1264035953933156432>Veilocity</span> <span class=chatlog__timestamp title="Sunday, May 24, 2026 1:56 PM"><a href=#chatlog__message-container-1508046001162813471>5/24/2026 1:56 PM</a></span></div><div class="chatlog__content chatlog__markdown"><span class=chatlog__markdown-preserve><strong>Independent Children’s Lawyer Information Submission &amp; Contextual Parenting Concerns - 10/09/2024</strong>

This material relates to the submission of an Independent Children’s Lawyer (ICL) Information Form by Stephen Cooke during ongoing family law proceedings concerning parenting arrangements for Christian and Joshua Cooke. The email exchange reflects procedural difficulties surrounding the submission of extensive supporting material, including repeated requests to reduce or limit information to the narrow scope of the form itself despite Stephen attempting to provide broader contextual material he believed relevant to the children’s welfare and the surrounding family dynamics. The documents contain detailed information regarding the children’s health, education, emotional wellbeing, extracurricular activities, and parenting arrangements, alongside concerns regarding communication breakdowns, exclusion from aspects of the children’s care, and the broader emotional impact of the separation on the children. Supporting records include medical and psychological reports, school assessments, parenting course certificates, and extensive timeline evidence documenting Stephen’s active participation in the boys’ upbringing, daily routines, medical care, education, and extracurricular commitments.</span></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1508046001917923508/6-9-2024_-_ICL_Information_Form_-_Father.pdf?ex=6a2dd208&amp;is=6a2c8088&amp;hm=13aa5e9eb9f2d5591b4f4ee092026d7db2d29d307aa77bcf800f0eef91bcffca&amp;"> 6-9-2024_-_ICL_Information_Form_-_Father.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>41.19 MB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1508046002186227844/EMAIL_-_Independent_Childrens_Lawyer_Information_Submission__Contextual_Parenting_Concerns.pdf?ex=6a2dd209&amp;is=6a2c8089&amp;hm=bc575de8876f859b3bd90ca567cf64edaabc9e5e01646c79b6aad07a5b8799d7&amp;"> EMAIL_-_Independent_Childrens_Lawyer_Information_Submission__Contextual_Parenting_Concerns.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>999.08 KB</div></div></div></div></div></div></div>
<div class=chatlog__message-group><div id=chatlog__message-container-1508047906333265940 class=chatlog__message-container data-message-id=1508047906333265940><div class=chatlog__message><div class=chatlog__message-aside><img class=chatlog__avatar src=https://cdn.discordapp.com/embed/avatars/4.png alt=Avatar loading=lazy></div><div class=chatlog__message-primary><div class=chatlog__header><span class=chatlog__author title=dadventuressteve data-user-id=1264035953933156432>Veilocity</span> <span class=chatlog__timestamp title="Sunday, May 24, 2026 2:03 PM"><a href=#chatlog__message-container-1508047906333265940>5/24/2026 2:03 PM</a></span></div><div class="chatlog__content chatlog__markdown"><span class=chatlog__markdown-preserve><strong>Delay in Release of Court-Ordered Property Settlement Funds 23/09/2024</strong>

This email exchange concerns delays in the release of court-ordered property settlement funds following final consent orders made in the Cooke family law proceedings in September 2024. Stephen Cooke sought the prompt release of funds allocated to him under the Court Orders after Ramsden Family Law confirmed receipt of sale proceeds from the former matrimonial property. The correspondence highlights frustration surrounding the requirement for consent and response from Delaney Roberts Specialist Family Lawyers before trust funds could be distributed, despite the orders appearing finalized and unambiguous. Ramsden Family Law explained their legal obligations regarding trust monies and inability to act unilaterally without engagement from the opposing party. The exchange reflects Stephen’s growing concern regarding ongoing procedural delays, additional legal expense, and perceived obstruction preventing timely compliance with Court Orders, including discussions about potential enforcement action and complaints regarding the handling of the matter.</span></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1508047906383466646/EMAIL_-_Delay_in_Release_of_Court-Ordered_Property_Settlement_Funds.pdf?ex=6a2dd3cf&amp;is=6a2c824f&amp;hm=b40d5e5b9f60eed7fa942cf94ae403da1aa2f8e119ead23881a640cac0b65076&amp;"> EMAIL_-_Delay_in_Release_of_Court-Ordered_Property_Settlement_Funds.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>486.46 KB</div></div></div></div></div></div></div>
<div class=chatlog__message-group><div id=chatlog__message-container-1508051377421680741 class=chatlog__message-container data-message-id=1508051377421680741><div class=chatlog__message><div class=chatlog__message-aside><img class=chatlog__avatar src=https://cdn.discordapp.com/embed/avatars/4.png alt=Avatar loading=lazy></div><div class=chatlog__message-primary><div class=chatlog__header><span class=chatlog__author title=dadventuressteve data-user-id=1264035953933156432>Veilocity</span> <span class=chatlog__timestamp title="Sunday, May 24, 2026 2:17 PM"><a href=#chatlog__message-container-1508051377421680741>5/24/2026 2:17 PM</a></span></div><div class="chatlog__content chatlog__markdown"><span class=chatlog__markdown-preserve><strong>Family Report Proceedings, Affidavit Filing &amp; Co-Parenting Proposal – Cooke v Cooke 27/11/2024</strong>

This material concerns ongoing parenting proceedings in the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia relating to the preparation of a Single Expert Family Report in the matter of Cooke v Cooke. The documents include correspondence between Stephen Cooke, Delaney Roberts Family Lawyers, and JLM Family Lawyers regarding the exchange of material intended for Family Report Writer Drew Cowen. Stephen Cooke served an Application in a Proceeding and supporting affidavit seeking leave to provide additional contextual material directly to the Family Report Writer, including medical records, subpoenaed documents, and evidence relating to his parenting capacity, financial stability, and home environment. The affidavit raised concerns regarding transparency, procedural fairness, and the selective flow of information through opposing parties. The material also records Stephen’s proposal for a collaborative 50/50 co-parenting arrangement focused on the best interests of the children, while alternatively supporting continuation of the Family Report process to ensure the expert had broader context available when forming recommendations.</span></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1508051377689989160/EMAIL_-_Family_Report_Proceedings_Affidavit_Filing__Co-Parenting_Proposal.pdf?ex=6a2dd70a&amp;is=6a2c858a&amp;hm=68a9b3f6841b4e83c6def92476eb613ecf752f3a9ed23fcae4fa449987f54eb0&amp;"> EMAIL_-_Family_Report_Proceedings_Affidavit_Filing__Co-Parenting_Proposal.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>612.56 KB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1508051378084511794/Affidavit_P_NCC3896_2023_14193403.pdf?ex=6a2dd70a&amp;is=6a2c858a&amp;hm=a7309798c1067adb8bedf811bd8a83f1dada696d4d9abd9c8a755d31895f2e8b&amp;"> Affidavit_P_NCC3896_2023_14193403.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>7.04 MB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1508051378659135558/Application_P_NCC3896_2023_14193402.pdf?ex=6a2dd70a&amp;is=6a2c858a&amp;hm=71b73c36f0603c955fbf8c223bfbfd0f0c589288cbb9656115cdaac5b0b7d0cb&amp;"> Application_P_NCC3896_2023_14193402.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>1.58 MB</div></div></div></div></div></div></div>
<div class=chatlog__message-group><div id=chatlog__message-container-1508063533513048094 class=chatlog__message-container data-message-id=1508063533513048094><div class=chatlog__message><div class=chatlog__message-aside><img class=chatlog__avatar src=https://cdn.discordapp.com/embed/avatars/4.png alt=Avatar loading=lazy></div><div class=chatlog__message-primary><div class=chatlog__header><span class=chatlog__author title=dadventuressteve data-user-id=1264035953933156432>Veilocity</span> <span class=chatlog__timestamp title="Sunday, May 24, 2026 3:06 PM"><a href=#chatlog__message-container-1508063533513048094>5/24/2026 3:06 PM</a></span></div><div class="chatlog__content chatlog__markdown"><span class=chatlog__markdown-preserve><strong>Self-Representation, Parenting Capacity &amp; Family Report Proceedings 05/11/2024</strong>

These materials relate to the ongoing family law proceedings in NCC3896/2023 between Stephen Christopher Cooke and Heather Anne Cooke, particularly surrounding parenting arrangements, dispute resolution, financial proceedings, and the preparation of the Family Report. The documents demonstrate Stephen Cooke’s transition to self-representation following concerns that critical evidence, including psychiatric records and drug and alcohol testing, was not being adequately presented to the Court or Family Report writer. The material includes Certificates of Dispute Resolution, affidavits, subpoenas, medical records, hair follicle testing, notices of ceasing legal representation, and correspondence regarding the joint letter of instruction to Family Report writer Drew Cowen. The records emphasize Stephen’s efforts to demonstrate sobriety compliance, ADHD treatment management, parenting involvement, emotional support for the children, educational engagement, stable housing, church and community participation, and support for a 50/50 co-parenting arrangement. The documents also reflect procedural tensions, extensive litigation pressures, financial strain, and Stephen’s assertion that self-representation became necessary to ensure the broader context and supporting evidence were fully considered in determining the children’s best interests.</span></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=chatlog__attachment-generic-icon><use href=#attachment-icon /></svg><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-name><a href="https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1466356241738760202/1508063534129483948/05-12-2023_-SC_-_Financial_Statement.pdf?ex=6a2de25d&amp;is=6a2c90dd&amp;hm=04a0e508c5cec71a6de56caefcd87efedf64dbd61b3f50ddc540bd1a0cb00729&amp;"> 05-12-2023_-SC_-_Financial_Statement.pdf </a></div><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic-size>363.47 KB</div></div></div><div class=chatlog__attachment><div class=chatlog__attachment-generic><svg class=ch